WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.060
Will drinking coffee give you cancer?

00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:04.360
According to the state of California it might.

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:08.960
They might be putting warning labels on coffee
that it contains a cancer causing chemical

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:10.680
what's your reaction to that?

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:13.400
Uh, I mean it's pretty crazy, I mean what's
that trope?

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:15.420
Nowadays every says everything will give you
cancer.

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:19.280
You can't treat adult people like they're,
I don't know, babies.

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:22.940
I appreciate a state government that cares
about it's people,

00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:25.560
I love California, I'm very happy that this
is my adopted state,

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:28.020
but that's ridiculous.

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:32.140
California Proposition 65 is an extensive
regulation

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:35.680
continuously changing to meet the demands
of consumer safety.

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:41.240
Thanks to Prop 65 enacted in 1986 businesses
are required to post a warning

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:45.860
about the presence of any substance known
by the state's Environmental Hazard Office

00:00:45.860 --> 00:00:48.860
to cause cancer or reproductive toxicity.

00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:53.820
The list is updated yearly and it now contains
more than 800 substances

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:57.800
almost everywhere you look in California there's
a Prop 65 warning.

00:00:57.800 --> 00:01:01.000
Apartment buildings, restaurants, even Disneyland.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:03.040
What are some of the places where you've seen
those?

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:03.780
Restaurants.

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:09.620
Yeah restaurants or like different stores
that might be microwave food.

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:13.400
See 'em like at the Echo Park Pool where I
go swimming.

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:17.380
When I see one of those signs it doesn't make
me thing twice about the establishment

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:19.100
because I see them everywhere.

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:23.820
So I recognize that it's kind of a blanket
attempt to protect people

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:25.160
perhaps from themselves.

00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:27.800
And a recent ruling from a Los Angeles judge

00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:30.880
orders major coffee chains like Starbucks and Pete's

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:35.260
to post explicit warnings that chemicals in
coffee might cause cancer.

00:01:35.260 --> 00:01:38.460
We stationed ourselves near a coffee shop
in Los Angeles

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:41.880
and asked people how far they think labeling
should go.

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:46.620
I'm glad they care, I'm still gonna be slamming
cold brew pretty regularly

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:50.480
and that may be what ends me but I'll go very
alert.

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:51.619
Does it give cancer?

00:01:51.620 --> 00:01:53.560
I'm about to get some right now.

00:01:53.560 --> 00:01:58.740
Acrylamide and appears on California's list

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:02.500
because studies show that lab rats are more
likely to develop cancer

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:05.840
when administered extremely high doses of
the chemical.

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:11.100
A human being would need to drink approximately
35 thousand cups of coffee

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:16.100
or a mere 16 thousand cups of instant coffee
a day for life

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:18.140
to reach those Acrylamide levels.

00:02:18.140 --> 00:02:21.720
I'm not gonna drink that much, just a cup.

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:25.300
And the World Health Organization has said
there's inadequate evidence

00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:28.360
that coffee drinking increases cancer risk.

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:29.660
If it makes people feel better

00:02:29.660 --> 00:02:33.980
and if it makes some representative feel like
they did their job that's good for them,

00:02:33.980 --> 00:02:37.360
but I think most of us are going to continue
drinking a lot of coffee.

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:40.920
It's gonna get to where there's going to have
to be signs on the air, air causes cancer.

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:42.180
It's like, any-

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:43.180
It does though.

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:44.240
I know that's what I'm saying!

00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:48.400
Some other chemicals on the list include Formaldehyde
and Arsenic

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:51.520
the latter of which occurs naturally in apples.

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:53.960
Should apples be labeled as containing Arsenic?

00:02:53.970 --> 00:02:56.480
I mean you're not gonna be able to label an
apple tree,

00:02:56.480 --> 00:03:00.110
I mean the tree comes from the ground, comes
from the soil it's probably that.

00:03:00.110 --> 00:03:01.110
In the grocery store?

00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:04.200
In the grocery store, yeah, like an individual
label I don't know

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:05.940
but on like a bag of apples, sure.

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:10.160
Apples don't actually have to be labelled
because the chemical occurs naturally

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:14.640
rather than as a byproduct of human intervention,
an exception in the law.

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:17.500
Is there any danger in like over warning,

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:22.140
if people do become numb to things that aren't
necessarily serious harms

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:24.120
and they ignore, like, the real warning.

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:25.480
Yeah I guess I could see your point there

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:28.600
because I see warnings all the time I never
really pay attention to them.

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:33.880
It goes in here and out there, I mean so its,
I don't take it serious at all.

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:37.440
Besides the possibility of numbing citizens
to real dangers

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:39.740
over warning brings other costs

00:03:39.740 --> 00:03:45.100
such as those to business owners who are regularly
sued for failing to post adequate signage.

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:49.600
One trade association estimates that the typical
non compliance lawsuit settlement

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:52.520
to be 65,000 dollars per item.

00:03:52.520 --> 00:03:55.280
What about the costs that it imposes on the
businesses

00:03:55.290 --> 00:04:01.220
because they would have to actually test,
in a lab their food, a little deli counter

00:04:01.220 --> 00:04:04.450
do you worry about, you know, maybe that effecting
the price

00:04:04.450 --> 00:04:06.820
for people who need access to fresh food?

00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:11.240
I didn't think about that but I don't know.

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:13.700
You think it's worth it, though?

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:15.400
Yeah I think it's worth it.

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:19.140
And cancer warnings aren't the only labels
that are required in California.

00:04:19.140 --> 00:04:23.060
The state also mandates calorie counts in
fast food restaurants.

00:04:23.060 --> 00:04:26.520
This idea proved much more popular than the
people we spoke with.

00:04:26.520 --> 00:04:30.600
Nutritional labeling makes sense because it's
just telling me about content

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:32.900
it's not making a moral judgement for me.

00:04:32.900 --> 00:04:37.400
I absolutely enjoy it because I will instantly
look at the caloric intake

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:39.370
because that's become very educational.

00:04:39.370 --> 00:04:40.760
I guess it's good for some people,

00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:44.940
I obviously don't count too many calories
but-

00:04:44.940 --> 00:04:48.620
But a recent report on nutritional labeling
from the USDA

00:04:48.620 --> 00:04:52.680
concludes that the best designed studies show
that calorie labels

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:56.080
do not reduce total calories ordered at restaurants.

00:04:56.080 --> 00:04:59.860
We are educated to the point now that we know
that everything is an issue

00:04:59.870 --> 00:05:03.120
you know everything can cause something or
do something to us.

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:06.320
I mean there is a problem with like eating
disorders and stuff like that

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:10.000
and I think that that kind of labeling just
makes that worse.

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:14.500
The California Department of Health has proposed
rules to require calorie counts

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:16.560
anywhere that serves food

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:19.760
including deli counters and grocery stores.

00:05:19.760 --> 00:05:23.700
Does that worry you at all that that puts
a burden on the smaller businesses

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:25.720
to have to comply with that kind of labeling?

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:30.740
No it's just finding managers and people who
are capable and willing to take part in this.

00:05:30.740 --> 00:05:32.700
If I want to go someplace I'm gonna go someplace,

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:36.960
warnings are a good thing but if I want to
go to the haunted mansion I'm going to go

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:38.560
and I'm gonna get coffee while I'm there.

00:05:38.560 --> 00:05:44.240
An increasingly popular idea is the mandatory
labeling of genetically modified foods.

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:46.260
Do you know if this has GMOs in it?

00:05:46.260 --> 00:05:48.800
You have to scan that new code on the back.

00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:49.540
Really?

00:05:49.540 --> 00:05:55.120
A ballot proposition requiring GMO labeling
failed by only three percentage points in California

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:57.800
and other states like Connecticut, Vermont
and Maine

00:05:57.800 --> 00:06:00.420
have actually passed GMO labeling laws.

00:06:00.420 --> 00:06:04.940
Scientists have produced no evidence that
GMO foods cause harm to humans.

00:06:04.940 --> 00:06:07.180
I think GMO labeling is helpful.

00:06:07.180 --> 00:06:11.060
Again, people can have informed consent, they
can decide what they want to do.

00:06:11.060 --> 00:06:14.080
So how much labeling is too much labeling?

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:17.620
The state of California seems right on track
to test that question.

00:06:17.620 --> 00:06:22.680
If we're a laboratory state and other states
can look to us and see what worked and what didn't

00:06:22.680 --> 00:06:25.600
that's fine by me, it's at least an interesting
place to live.

00:06:25.600 --> 00:06:28.480
I don't always love what happens here but
I'm never bored.

